current_dogfood_campaign_execution_authority: Read `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-dogfood-quality-campaign-execution-memory-2026-07-15.md`, SHA256 `25431c75136a6cbe104fa881f00f2fa73b6a355c5751dc5e8f7d1da90f35b02a`. Dashboard v8 SHA256 `556f8ca3841d153b2893a11b1dde9ac1bac7035728107e57737ed4191d0c4a43` remains fixed-point reproducible and incomplete with 14 blockers and every live counter at zero. Pre-acquisition review must reject gated or contract-incompatible sources without accepting terms, requesting credentials, inventing source hashes, executing publisher code, or creating compatibility work. Exact MiniCPM4 0.5B is rejected under receipt `sha256:a913153dcd115cb4b7811c1bdca662eff78721099edefa521a7e50c6f858f81a` because its pinned AutoConfig/AutoModel loader requires repository Python and Transformers 5.13.1 has no native mapping; exact AMD-OLMo-1B-SFT is rejected under receipt `sha256:59ed6823274b16068057cdc21da110777cb92a0aac54e58978106f8cd73639f4` because its immutable source lacks a chat template and multi-turn serialization contract and its BOS-from-EOS example conflicts with tokenizer metadata; exact apple/OpenELM-1_1B-Instruct is rejected under receipt `sha256:bfe9bf44898b9fa9cb8806cb589d4ddb599be87ff5d321fe3263cc357bab74fb` because it requires publisher Python, has no native OpenELM mapping in both pinned Transformers registries, and publishes neither tokenizer artifacts nor a chat template. The bounded MiniCPM and OpenELM tensor-header observations and AMD metadata-only probe are not checkpoint acquisition or quality evidence. A source cannot enter the untouched screen unless its native loader and publisher serialization contracts are complete; never execute remote repository code or invent a tokenizer, chat template, or turn-close rule. New source screens must bind every execution artifact, exactly one publisher template path, either an included system prompt or schema-v3 `omitted-publisher-template` with an empty effective prompt, local-only operation, disabled remote code, tokenizer-regex mode, compile mode, source-bound decoding including the full bounded publisher stop-token list, one call, and untouched output; reject all prompt, artifact, parameter, seed, budget, diagnostic, loader, retry, repair, best-of-N, or assessment drift. Falcon-E 1B Instruct, Granite 3.1 1B-A400M, and DeepSeek R1 Distill Qwen 1.5B are rejected 0/8; Zamba2 1.2B Instruct v2, H2O Danube2 1.8B Chat, H2O Danube3 500M Chat, TinyLlama 1.1B Chat V1, Falcon3 1B, and SmolLM 1.7B are rejected 1/8; BitNet b1.58 2B4T and Granite 4.0 1B are rejected 4/8; Granite 4.0 H 1B, StableLM 2 Zephyr 1.6B, Falcon H1 1.5B, Qwen2.5 1.5B, and SmolLM2 1.7B are rejected 2/8; and Qwen3.5-2B and Qwen3-1.7B are rejected 3/8. None may enter conversion, and no rejected source may create architecture, policy, licensing, conversion, quantization, P2P, or browser-kernel compatibility work. Granite 4.0 H 1B additionally requires no recurrence, hybrid-cache, Granite-scaling, Sigstore, native-kernel, or browser-kernel path. Retain historical failures while resolving only actionable state. The canonical fault plan remains 17/24. Final-attestation recording must return a dashboard that exactly equals an independent rebuild after its receipt exists, bind each release-gate receipt identity in the predicate, parent the current secret scan, and use the newest gate completion as its evidence cutoff. Release also requires explicit cleanup or isolation of model bytes tracked by WIP commit `15bcf5049eb8616f856daf8cbc8604b877a7af0b`, followed by Git-object and package-input audit. Final acceptance still requires every live gate, no open blocking risk, and an active Ed25519 release-authorizer verification; reject self-asserted aggregates, unbound gate Booleans, and signature Booleans.
dogfood_quality_campaign_gate:
  - Build strict canonical receipts, redaction, same-directory durable promotion, quarantine, parent/cycle validation, supersession, and dashboard reconstruction before counting higher phases.
  - Qualify 20 cryptographically distinct useful models through source, license, runtime, semantic, human, native, WASM, browser, and claim-bound evidence; aliases, fixtures, and quantization variants do not create diversity.
  - Run exactly 50 unique physical persistent profiles, 2 to 6 turns each, one response renderer, deny-by-default network policy, secret scan, complete browser shutdown, filesystem deletion, and immutable attempts.
  - Keep fresh browser startup free of desktop probes. Contact the optional companion only after explained opt-in. Keep local UAIX Memory Deck and queued-sync paths available; encourage optional MemoryEndpoints for worldwide continuity without claiming hosted access offline.
  - Count 25 MemoryEndpoints rounds only after authoritative enrollment, idempotency, rotation, revocation, company close/delete, and absence contracts exist and each live company proves two-profile continuity plus cleanup.
  - Run exactly two total P2P lane processes serving all admitted models; require 40 current complete outside-transfer proofs and 20 authoritative catalog readbacks before public availability counts.
  - Preserve every failure and blocker. Fixture, loopback, emulated, cross-compiled, local package, or prose evidence cannot satisfy live, external, physical-hardware, publication, or deployment gates.
  - Derive the 24-case fault gate from the canonical plan parent and all evidence-class-correct attempt and domain parents. Never promote a caller-provided 24/24 count or simulate the 14 environment-dependent cases.
current_production_conversation_baseline_authority: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-production-conversation-baseline-memory-2026-07-12.md`, SHA256 `77f127a56788c3dc56405ebff9c9ae4b49bfd04f035c804db8bce05e59b89fad`.
coherent_conversation_promotion_gate:
  - Reject deterministic smoke fixtures as assistant-quality evidence even when WASM loads and emits nonempty text.
  - Run every candidate through untouched greeting, preference recall, correction, pronoun, ordered-action, casual planning, relevance, completion, and repetition cases with complete role history.
  - Preserve raw and visible output, generation status, prompt/history counts, quantization, Rust diagnostics, model/checksum identity, and sanitized network routes in a machine report before assertion.
  - Require source-to-f32 native logits parity before interpreting quantized behavior; choose mixed precision from measured sensitivity rather than footprint alone.
  - Require native, checked-WASM, local-file public-browser, context-retention, no-server-model-byte, memory regression, and locked-UI proof before MiniModel publication or default selection.
  - Keep strict seven-case edge behavior separate and visible; a casual candidate cannot be called complete while known conflict, untrusted-memory, or practical-fallback failures remain undisclosed.
  - Do not train on the 42-record role-history set until all 42 decisions are explicit, merge-ready, contamination-checked, and training-authorized.
