browser_prefix_cache_performance_gate:
  - Prove first-turn reuse is zero and computed prompt tokens equal the full prompt count.
  - Prove a repeated-turn prompt reuses only a complete exact retained-token prefix with cache length equal to that prefix and computes a nonempty suffix.
  - Prove partial prefix, changed prefix, empty suffix, model load, adapter apply, reset, and generation failure cannot reuse stale KV state.
  - Compare reused-path final logits bit-for-bit with a fresh full prefill and compare strict visible/raw outputs byte-for-byte with the prior checked runtime.
  - Require runtime/workspace/fmt/clippy, Node contracts, checked-WASM ABI, .NET package, memory verifier, static/HTTP browser harness, real two-turn browser smoke, and unchanged UI evidence.
  - Treat latency and binary-size measurements as performance evidence only; they cannot change a semantic rubric, promote a model, or authorize deployment.
  - Before production status, require atomic release, public HTTPS WASM byte/hash readback, live two-turn diagnostics, and rollback evidence.
