available_now:
  - CURRENT single-use agent enrollment gate: create a fresh company/workspace per live run; issue one opaque expiring URL; require first POST claim to atomically persist one canonical agent name/token and consume the URL; then submit the byte-identical URL with a distinct idempotency key and require HTTP 409/410 typed consumed safe no-op. Same-key retry may recover the original lost response but cannot create another authority. Prove one agent/token/package/receipt, name+token reconnect from clean browser state, exact 12-record virtual-UAIX startup order, latest short-term plus bounded long-term pointer restore, rotation/revocation, wrong-agent and cross-tenant rejection, TinyRustLM.com CORS, zero invitation/token persistence, and automatic redacted backend defect posting on replay success. From `finally`, require separate close and delete operations for every created company; attempt delete even if close fails; a run cannot pass without both redacted receipts, and cleanup failure posts `test_company_cleanup_failed`. Missing advertised capability is blocked, never skipped or passed.
  - CURRENT strict conversation-quality gate: use `one-call-conversation-quality-v1`, source-greedy decoding, complete role-preserving history, at most six prior turns, untouched output, and separate integrity versus quality status. Reject retries, output prefixes, repairs, field assembly, expected-answer injection, and keyword-only promotion. Require 7/7 semantic passes for latest correction, pronoun/reference resolution, ordered actions, authoritative conflict confirmation, untrusted-memory precedence plus current-task continuation, latest units, and feasible constrained fallback. The exact fixture SHA256 is `161d50b3ac8821f9262350196b081dfe19ceb0c92a3d212b500aa1678e6d8066`; it must be an immutable training exclusion. Current q4 is 3/7; every tested larger source/prompt/few-shot/adapter candidate is at or below 4/7 and rejected.
  - CURRENT multi-turn conversation gate: require only complete stable user/assistant pairs; exclude active, stopped, rejected, failed, and incomplete turns; keep chronological role order; retain at most six newest whole turns; neutralize embedded template-control tokens; render exact selected-model ChatML/Qwen/raw boundaries; reserve output capacity; and evict oldest whole turns under both manifest context length and the outer 4 KiB module-plan cap. Keep calculator and specialized field helpers single-turn unless separately designed and tested. Run all Node tests, JS syntax, static-shell parity, Rust fmt/clippy/workspace tests, .NET solution tests, registered `multi-turn-context` real browser smoke, MemoryEndpoints browser regression, report-intake verification, and `git diff --check`. Require real second-turn recall, prompt-token growth, `conversation_history_turns=1`, q4 diagnostics, local-only network routes, and no duplicate response rendering. Do not weaken or rewrite the visual baseline; resolve the current mobile open-versus-closed advanced-drawer expectation through explicit human visual review.
  - CURRENT q5 runtime and admission gate: require q5 element counts divisible by eight, exact five-byte payloads per eight signed codes, positive finite per-block scales, checked payload/scale lengths, no f32 tensor shadows, native matvec parity, q5 generation, q5 sparse/low-rank adapter coverage, public `.slm` inspection, optimized WASM build, q8 and q5 ABI smokes with explicit recovery quantization, corrupt-scale rejection, full workspace rustfmt/clippy/tests, 123 .NET tests, 28 browser contracts, protected five-package/five-symbol audit, and clean consumer install. Keep `mixed-q5-matrix-f32-norm-v1` experimental while it remains 4/8 source argmax or lacks same-artifact prefill/decode latency proof. Reject selector/default/browser promotion and do not restore the larger sensitive-block32 or q8-edge/q5-body profiles without new measured evidence.
  - CURRENT browser virtual-UAIX and notification gate: require strict Rust/C#/browser parsing of `memoryendpoints.virtual_uai_contract.v1`, exact 12-path order, 64 KiB bounds, exposure flags, workspace-scoped agent name recovery, memory-only credentials, 0/12 setup-required behavior, one-record writes, authoritative startup readback, `expectedRevision`, explicit conflicts, no silent promotion, and `saved locally; synchronization pending` before receipts. Require deterministic `current-message` cursor pagination, `responseRequired` handling, meeting-room response readback before acknowledgement, idempotent stale-unread reconciliation, multi-tab single-writer proof, restart/lost-IndexedDB recovery, tenant negatives, and secret scans. Polling is authority; SSE is an optional hint only. Preserve the locked UI.
  - CURRENT malformed-logit and runtime-architecture gate: require greedy and stochastic tests that reject NaN and positive infinity, preserve negative infinity only as an intentional suppression sentinel, preserve finite tie and seeded behavior, and return `GenerationFailed` when no finite candidate remains. Run Rust formatting, focused sampler tests, full runtime tests, optimized `wasm32-unknown-unknown` build, and WASM ABI smoke. Treat the 13 MemoryEndpoints architecture pages as proposed until code and tests prove each one. Before browser-loading claims, require exact pre-allocation budgets, bounded OPFS/worker ownership, mediated network policy, cancellation/restart/multi-tab tests, Chrome/Firefox/Safari capability fallback, and atomic last-known-good rollback. Raising the current 256 MiB transfer cap alone is not acceptance for the 602,862,400-byte fidelity candidate.
